To configure Decision Center to look on a different App server for the SSP, you need to create your own SSP resolver and add it to the teamserver.war. Here are the steps:

1. Pack all your XOMs (eXecutable Object Model) into the ssp.war following the documentation [http://publib.boulder.ibm.com/infocenter/brjrules/v7r1/topic/com.ibm.websphere.ilog.jrules.doc/Content/Business_Rules/Documentation/_pubskel/JRules/ps_JRules_Global720.html].
2. Deploy the SSP (ssp.war) on each server along with a XU connection factory and the appropriate datasource definition.
3. Create your own SSP resolver by implementing the IlrSSPResolver interface, specifically the getSSPURL(String serverName, URL url) method. This method will allow you to point to a different server URL.
4. Add your custom SSP resolver to the teamserver.war.
5. Set the teamserver.defaultSSPResolver.class property to your custom SSP resolver class.

For example, you can have 2 servers defined in RTS:
* testingServer1 http://host1:9080/res
* testingServer2 http://host1:9080/res

And your SSP provider can evaluate the SSP URL as follows:
```java
if (serverName.equals("testingServer1")) {
    return (new URL("http://server1:9000/testing"));
} else if (serverName.equals("testingServer2")) {
    return (new URL("http://server2:9000/testing"));
} else {
    return (new URL("http://host1:9000/testing"));
}
```
In your case, you can configure the SSP resolver to point to the runtime server (with port 9000) instead of the management server (with port 8000).

Note: Make sure to check the server logs for any error messages and ensure that the SSP is correctly deployed and configured. Also, ensure that the HTTP port is not being used by another process. 

Additionally, you can refer to the Clustering Decision Validation Services documentation [http://www.ibm.com/support/docview.wss?uid=swg21425487] for more details on configuring the SSP and RES management console on different servers. 

It is also recommended to check the application server console to ensure that the application EAR files for the Decision Center and the RES Management are deployed and have been started, and to check the HTTP port number and ensure that it is not being used by another process. 

Please refer to the IlrSSPResolver documentation [http://publib.boulder.ibm.com/infocenter/brjrules/v7r1/index.jsp?topic=/com.ibm.websphere.ilog.jrules.doc/html/api/html/ilog/rules/teamserver/model/testing/IlrSSPResolver.html] for more information on creating a custom SSP resolver. 

The product versions mentioned in the passages are 8.6, 8.5, 8.0, and 7.5 of IBM Operational Decision Manager. 

The error message you are encountering is "the host and port are responsive but the "/testing/sspService" cannot be found", which is expected if the SSP is not deployed on the same server as the RES console. 

By following these steps and configuring your custom SSP resolver, you should be able to configure Decision Center to look on a different App server for the SSP.
